==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|penaunce}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|peneance}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|paenitentia||penitence}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpɛn.əns/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-penance.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A voluntary self-imposed [[punishment]] for a [[sinful]] act or wrongdoing. It may be intended to serve as [[reparation]] for the act.
#* Coleridge
#*: Quoth he, "The man hath '''penance''' done, / And penance more will do."
# A [[sacrament]] in some Christian churches.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[repentance]]
#: {{rfquotek|Wyclif Bible (Luke xv. 7)}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[pain]]; [[sorrow]]; [[suffering]]
#* Chaucer
#*: Joy or '''penance''' he feeleth none.

